1
00:00:01,950 --> 00:00:06,210
Adding an application into Aosp build system is pretty straightforward.

2
00:00:06,210 --> 00:00:13,110
Let's have a look at the steps to add Java and Kotlin apps to the Aosp build system.

3
00:00:13,110 --> 00:00:15,590
There are two ways to add apps.

4
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:21,990
One is to add the complete project with the source code into the Aosp build system.

5
00:00:21,990 --> 00:00:29,220
The second option is to add a compiled APK file, so that means you will create the project in a separate

6
00:00:29,220 --> 00:00:29,850
IDE.

7
00:00:29,880 --> 00:00:37,020
For example, Android studio and you will build the project and make the APK and only move the APK into

8
00:00:37,020 --> 00:00:38,740
the Aosp folder.

9
00:00:38,760 --> 00:00:46,860
So in this session we are going to look at point one and see how to add a complete Android project with

10
00:00:46,860 --> 00:00:48,540
source code into aosp.

11
00:00:48,570 --> 00:00:56,040
The reason why we cannot simply copy the Android project directly into Aosp is due to the fact that

12
00:00:56,040 --> 00:00:58,520
both uses different build system.

13
00:00:58,530 --> 00:01:06,480
As we know, the Android application uses gradle build system and Aosp uses the song build system.

14
00:01:06,480 --> 00:01:10,510
These two build systems are not compatible with each other.

15
00:01:10,530 --> 00:01:15,660
That's the reason we have to do some manual migration steps in between.

16
00:01:15,660 --> 00:01:20,620
So these are the steps to migrate an Android project into Aosp.

17
00:01:20,640 --> 00:01:24,400
So first step is to restructure the folders.

18
00:01:24,420 --> 00:01:31,740
That means we need to just extract the Java or Kotlin source folders and the resource folders from the

19
00:01:31,740 --> 00:01:37,500
Android project and rest of the Gradle files are not necessary for aosp.

20
00:01:37,530 --> 00:01:45,240
Second step the same android manifest dot xml can be copied into the Aosp folders.

21
00:01:45,240 --> 00:01:47,190
It doesn't need any changes.

22
00:01:47,220 --> 00:01:51,270
Third step is to write the song build scripts.

23
00:01:51,270 --> 00:01:58,390
So we need to write the standard BP file for the new project or the module we are going to add.

24
00:01:58,410 --> 00:02:04,380
First step include the new module or the project in corresponding build scripts.

25
00:02:04,380 --> 00:02:12,960
In the next sessions, we will do a couple of practical sessions to add a Kotlin and Java project into

26
00:02:12,990 --> 00:02:13,660
Aosp.

27
00:02:13,680 --> 00:02:19,860
So I am using the Android automotive build in this case, but the overall steps which we are following

28
00:02:19,860 --> 00:02:24,240
in these sessions are similar for other builds as well.

29
00:02:24,240 --> 00:02:30,240
So in case if you have a foreign build, please follow the similar steps and it should go fine.

